        "kind": "review",
        "ok": true,
        "reason": "I found no concrete defect in src/middleware/cache/index.ts. Every entry is stored under `<origin>/.hono/cache` with `__hono_cache_key` (fragment removed, never resolved as a URL) followed by `__hono_cache_method`; QUERY keys then add the SHA-256 body digest, the four content headers, and the Vary values. The body is read from a clone or from HonoRequest's body cache, so the handler still gets it. A body read as FormData bypasses caching, and so does one over `maxQueryBodySize` or one that can't be read; a body exactly at the limit is cached. Without Web Crypto, QUERY bypasses caching while GET still works, and `onCacheNotAvailable` gets the specified reason string once, when the middleware is created. I read the code but did not run the tests.",
